ut to sea  foreshadowing the deaths of  two characters later in the episode the  second is renault's 1795 painting the  genius of france between  liberty and death depicting an angel in  between a lady liberty on the left and  death on the right our captives are  stuck in a similar dilemma to this angel  held captive deprived of their liberty  on the one hand  and the specter of death on the other  atticus wants to find his father but  according to william he's on an errand  and won't be back till later they get a  tour of this creepy mansion  and its founder titus braithwight fun  fact braith comes from the old irish  word for betrayer notice here this  ring a symbol of the order of the  ancient dawn the secret society we'll  learn more about in a bit  titus apparently made his fortune in  shipping which letty surmises  involved the shipping of slaves as we'll  learn later titus did own slaves  impregnating one named hannah who  happens to be a great-great-grandmother  of atticus they decide to check out the  village of artem which looks like it's  run by the amish but find on their way  their car which was completely destroyed  the other night is  totally repaired notice how artem  utilizes a lot of  red from the barn to the flowers to the  kids playing whatever the hell this is  it's all to foreshadow danger atticus  hears a whistleblown the same sound he  heard that called off the shoghos the  previous night  it was blown by this woman who holds  sway over this creepy stone  silo a silo atticus believes may hold  his father  it's important to note that the whistle  is what makes ledy and george lose their  memory but atticus is impervious to it  on their way back to the manor as if  they didn't learn anything from the  previous night  they're saved from another attack by  none other than christina braithwight  the daughter of  samuel braithwight who we'll meet in a  bit atticus is taken to samuel's lab  where samuel's own organs are being  harvested for a dinner later in the  evening  it's okay however since samuel has the  ability to heal healing letty near the  end of the episode after shooting her  here we learn of a painting based off a  biblical verse in the book of genesis  this painting however was not painted by  a joseph tanhauser as samuel suggests  it's by john miles and it's called the  naming of the animals in which adam  helps god in creation by  creating a beautiful hierarchy of all  living things that no good eve arrived  however and tempted adam throwing the  hierarchy into a mess of tribes and  nations  now samuel here believes he can find a  way back to the garden of eden where  things are perfect and he can be  immortal he needs however ticks power  the blood of his ancestors  christina locks tick in his room with a  spell tick will later communicate with  george through the walls using morse  code calling their captors  wizards we'll also get this super odd  scene where christina delivers a baby  shogoth from a cow  i'm still scratching my head as to why  this scene was put in here as it really  doesn't advance the story but it's  possible the writers are setting  something up and need us to know that  these normal animals are being used as  vessels for abominable [ __ ] that can  later be controlled by christina i think  we definitely haven't seen the last of  her tick george and letty all experience  hallucinations as part of this secret  society's evening entertainment letty  makes out with a hallucination of  atticus only to find he's got a snake  penis  we get this shot of adam and eve adam  here also having a snake penis  and some have interpreted this story  from the bible as the snake symbolizing  satan  and the forbidden fruit as insemination  i didn't learn that in sunday school  george is visited by dora his brother's  wife it's  really hinted here that dora and him had  an affair and that this affair resulted  in the birth of atticus  making george atticus's real father  george even tells montrose that atticus  is  probably not his kid something the two  of them apparently settled years ago  further proof of this is when george  tells dora about a story he's writing  involving a man who reunites with his  long lost love  and they stay together before a house  collapses on them and what happens at  the end of this episode a house  collapses and  george dies allowing him to finally be  reunited with his long-lost love  dora who died before him the final  hallucination occurs between  tick and jia remember that girl tick  called from korea last episode  that's her she's also that red alien  thing that appeared in his dreams she is  really pissed at him and i can't help  but think that her anger is directly  related to the bad things  atticus said he did while fighting in  korea we aren't exactly sure what those  bad things are yet but we'll likely find  those out in future episodes it's really  interesting to note here that in the  subtitles it says that jia  isn't speaking korean but quote the  language of adam this is also the  language she probably spoke to him in  episode one  but i don't speak korean so i can't be  100 sure later in the episode christina  says the language of adam is so tricky  that  men have died trying to wield its power  i'm wondering if the book hannah escapes  with at the end of the episode contains  more information  about this powerful language this is  likely what george called the book of  names or the book of life it's the  opposite of the book of the dead the  necronomicon tick and george are invited  to dinner  sorry letty it's boys only no girls  allowed  there george recites the laws of their  ancient order in a book he found called  bylaws and precepts of the order of the  ancient dawn by their own law  regular members must obey orders from  those deemed sons  among sons those who are direct  descendants of titus braithwight  and since atticus is the last blood heir  he orders everyone to go home  so atticus letty and george head back to  that silo where they find montrose  having just escaped and if you're  looking for some nice tear-felt reunion  between father and son  you ain't gonna get it as they make  their escape in that silver sedan from  episode 1  we learn that this particular lodge is  one of many in a much  larger secret society this one is called  the sons of adam and years ago they  failed at conjuring a spell of  immortality which  killed everyone inside except of course  hannah their escape is short-lived  however when they smash headfirst into a  force field to make matters worse  samuel shoots letty and george he ends  up healing letty to prove to atticus  that he can heal  but won't heal george until he gets  atticus's help with his spell  sponge bath time christina tells atticus  of samuel's master plan to open a portal  to eden and there's a lot of talk about  changing destiny and even a social  commentary on how atticus was made a  member  solely based on his sex while christina  can never be a member because she's a  woman i think this is setting up her  character arc since samuel dies at the  end  i'm wondering if she'll try to take over  while george is on his deathbed we learn  a bit more about montrose's past he was  beaten by his father for liking to draw  montrose would later go on to beat  atticus for his love of books  it's a sad but revelatory bit of  information showing how trauma and abuse  can pass from one generation to the next  as atticus is forced to perform in this  experiment  a slave to his situation just like his  ancestors were actual slaves to theirs  gil scott heron's poem whitey on the  moon plays a poem which depicts the  plight of african americans  unable to pay medical bills and rent  when the government is spending millions  of their tax dollars on sending white  folks to the moon we are seeing  samuel's experiment at the expense of a  black man just like the progress of  space advancement was at the expense of  millions of black americans this  sentiment is also found in james  baldwin's speech from episode 1.  if you haven't checked out my video on  that i'll leave a link in the  description  as the experiment progresses a portal  opens with garden-like flowers  suggesting the garden of eden is  on the other side but before the  experiment goes completely haywire just  like it did decades ago  attica sees his great ancestor hannah  visibly pregnant on the other side we  also see this black  smoke-like essence emanate from  atticus's ring this seems to be the  energy that turns the others into stone  but why it comes out of the ring and why  it didn't turn atticus into stone  remains to be seen we do know that it  was charlotte who gave him this ring  leading me to believe she played a role  in sabotaging her father's plan  as retribution for keeping her on the  sidelines her entire life  because she's a woman i also just really  enjoyed the juxtaposition of atticus and  his great ancestor  escaping the home as it's destroyed in  their respective times but even though  atticus makes it out alive he finds out  his  uncle has passed leaving us wondering  what the heck will happen next now there  is an episode 3 preview which i've left  a link to in the description below  but even after watching that i'm still  scratching my head what the whole series  is working towards  thanks for watching everyone please make  sure to like and subscribe i'm planning  on breaking down  every episode of the series i'm also  interested to hear your thoughts in the  comments below  you can also follow me on twitter at  thingstoryt  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much
 

